                                "sense_id": "97b1f198-277b-323c-a6d9-4df01d1d3e3c",
                                "text": "Hushed into sweet tranquillity / By that divine dulciloquy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "063ac53b-f340-476d-a186-e9590853dcc6",
                                "sense_id": "97b1f198-277b-323c-a6d9-4df01d1d3e3c",
                                "text": "Winslow started on his dulciloquy. With an autocratic, barely perceptible sweep of the hand, the general cut him short."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d71f31b4-7223-4a9b-9592-8bd59ba2d5fc",
                                "sense_id": "97b1f198-277b-323c-a6d9-4df01d1d3e3c",
                                "text": "If Harrison's poetry depicts machine-gun tongues of fire as leading to nothing but apocalypse, a fruitless Pentecost, it does not commend the tongues of fire of dulciloquy and poetic eloquence as capable of bringing redemption."
                            }
                        ]
